@startuml
actor Learner
participant Web
participant "GotIt Backend" as Backend
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant "Reading-guide provider" as Provider
Learner -> Web: Open vocabulary
Web -> Backend: GET learning items
Backend --> Web: Owned source, meaning, cached phonetic fields
Web -> Backend: POST reading-guides {ids[1..30]}
Backend -> Backend: Authenticate; vocabulary.write; strict input
Backend -> DB: Resolve all owned non-deleted items and native preference
alt foreign or missing item
  Backend --> Web: 404; no provider call
else owned batch
  Backend -> Backend: Reuse matching cache; coalesce identical pending batch
  opt missing guides
    Backend -> Backend: Enforce AI quota
    Backend -> Provider: Bounded source/native-language request
    Provider --> Backend: Structured pronunciation guides
    Backend -> Backend: Validate IDs, length, script and output bounds
    Backend -> DB: Conditional write: owner/revision/source/native unchanged
  end
  Backend --> Web: Valid current guides only, or safe unavailable error
  Web --> Learner: Native guide below source; meaning beside source
end
note over Web,DB
No learning score or XP is generated.
Provider failure leaves optional guides absent.
end note
@enduml
